@startuml CyberSmart_Platform_Architecture

!define LIGHTBLUE #E3F2FD
!define LIGHTGREEN #E8F5E8
!define LIGHTYELLOW #FFF9C4
!define LIGHTPINK #FCE4EC
!define LIGHTGRAY #F5F5F5

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam roundcorner 15
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #2196F3
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1976D2
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam classBorderColor #666666

title CyberSmart Platform - System Architecture & User Journey

actor Student as student
participant "Streamlit\nDashboard" as dashboard LIGHTBLUE
participant "Assessment\nEngine" as assessment LIGHTGREEN
participant "ML Analysis\nSystem" as ml LIGHTYELLOW
participant "Local Storage\n(JSON)" as storage LIGHTGRAY
participant "GitHub\nIntegration" as github LIGHTPINK

== 1. Student Entry & Profile Creation ==
student -> dashboard: Access Platform
dashboard -> dashboard: Initialize Session
dashboard -> storage: Check/Create User Profile
storage --> dashboard: User Data Retrieved

== 2. Learning Assessment Phase ==
dashboard -> assessment: Start Cybersecurity Survey
assessment -> student: Present Knowledge Questions
student -> assessment: Submit Responses
assessment -> ml: Analyze Survey Responses
ml -> ml: Calculate Knowledge Score
ml --> assessment: Return Baseline Score
assessment -> storage: Store Survey Results
assessment --> dashboard: Display Initial Assessment

== 3. Interactive Learning Modules ==
dashboard -> student: Show Available Activities
alt Phishing Awareness Module
    student -> assessment: Select Phishing Game
    assessment -> student: Present Email Scenarios
    student -> assessment: Identify Phish/Legitimate
    assessment -> ml: Score Responses
    ml -> ml: Pattern Recognition Analysis
    ml --> assessment: Phishing Awareness Score
else Password Security Module  
    student -> assessment: Select Password Game
    assessment -> student: Present Password Scenarios
    student -> assessment: Create/Evaluate Passwords
    assessment -> ml: Analyze Password Strength
    ml -> ml: Entropy & Security Calculation
    ml --> assessment: Password Security Score
else Social Engineering Module
    student -> assessment: Select Social Engineering Quiz
    assessment -> student: Present Scenario Questions
    student -> assessment: Choose Best Responses
    assessment -> ml: Evaluate Responses
    ml --> assessment: Social Engineering Score
end

== 4. Real-time Analysis & Scoring ==
assessment -> ml: Compile All Activity Data
ml -> ml: Neural Network Processing
ml -> ml: Generate Comprehensive Scores
ml -> ml: Identify Strengths & Weaknesses
ml --> assessment: Detailed Analysis Results

== 5. Results & Personalized Recommendations ==
assessment -> dashboard: Send Analysis Results
dashboard -> dashboard: Generate Visualizations
dashboard -> student: Display Score Dashboard
dashboard -> student: Show Progress Charts
dashboard -> student: Provide Security Recommendations
dashboard -> student: Suggest Career Paths

== 6. Data Persistence & Reporting ==
dashboard -> storage: Save Session Results
storage -> storage: Update User Progress
storage -> github: Sync Reports (Optional)
github -> github: Store Aggregated Data
storage -> dashboard: Generate Progress Report
dashboard -> student: Email/Download Report

== 7. Continuous Learning Loop ==
dashboard -> student: Suggest Next Activities
student -> dashboard: Continue Learning Journey
note right: Platform tracks improvement\nover time and adapts\ncontent difficulty

@enduml